# Security headers (Cloudflare Pages / Netlify format).
#
# IMPORTANT: AWS CloudFront does NOT read this file. Production hosting is on
# S3 + CloudFront, where the same headers must be applied via a Response
# Headers Policy attached to the distribution. See infra/cloudfront-response-headers-policy.json
# for the canonical values to paste into the AWS console / Terraform.
#
# This file is kept for parity in case hosting ever migrates to Cloudflare or
# Netlify. It costs nothing on AWS — CloudFront ignores it.
#
# CSP intentionally NOT included: jQuery is inline, so a strict CSP needs
# unsafe-inline or per-tag hashes. Defer to a dedicated security pass.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
